  "overrides": {
    "maxDistanceMask": "0 cm on the top row (11 pinned vertices), 1000 cm elsewhere: the painted mask the brief asks for (the factory creates it all 0)",
    "collisionPhysicsAsset": "the body-only import's generated physics asset (see assets.bodyPhysicsAsset), not the caped mesh's",
    "visibilityBasedAnimTickOption": "AlwaysTickPoseAndRefreshBones: nothing renders offscreen, so bones must refresh unrendered (harness, not a cloth parameter)",
    "bWaitForParallelClothTask": "true: GetCurrentClothingData_GameThread requires it (harness, read-out only)",
    "capsuleRestClearance": "every capsule radius = min(stock radius, distance to the nearest rest cape vertex - 1 cm) on the Idle_Loop t = 0 pose, dropped under 0.1 cm (game.ts: measureBodyCapsules(capeSkin, 16, restWorld, COLLIDER_THICKNESS)); applied in RunDrive, in memory, restored after the run"
  },
  "determinism": "3 separate simulations (a fresh world and fresh clothing actors per run, CharDynProbe RunDrive); Chaos Cloth at a fixed step is deterministic, so the run files are byte-identical and the spread is 0",
  "differences": {
    "crossfade": "the game's AnimationPlayer smoothstep crossfade is replayed by UCharDynAnimInstance; Unreal blends the poses with FAnimationRuntime::BlendPosesTogether (normalised quaternion blend) where three.js accumulates slerps, and samples the Interchange-resampled clips",
    "readback": "Unreal reads the simulated positions every tick for the same tick's pose; the game reads a GPU readback every 2 frames and matches it to the pose of the step that produced it",
    "gravity": "-9.80 m/s^2 in Unreal, -9.81 m/s^2 in the game"
  },
  "hair": {
    "node": "FAnimNode_SpringBone, one per simulated bone (ponytail_2..6), parent first, each fed the previous node's pose, driven in UCharDynAnimInstance's proxy; ponytail_1 rides Head (SpringBoneChain3D's root)",
    "defaults": "stock (UE 5.8.3: Engine/Source/Runtime/AnimGraphRuntime/Private/BoneControllers/AnimNode_SpringBone.cpp:16-38): SpringStiffness 50, SpringDamping 4, ErrorResetThresh 256 cm, bLimitDisplacement false, translate X/Y/Z on, rotate X/Y/Z off; fixed step 1/120 s (:62-63); no gravity, no collision",
    "differences": "SpringBoneChain3D (game) keeps each segment at its rest length, rotates the bones toward the particles and pushes them out of the body capsules; the stock SpringBone translates the bone only, so segments stretch, and it has no collider. Its damping acts on the world velocity and OwnerVelocity is 0 for an actor's own component (AnimNode_SpringBone.cpp:139-157, 257-266), so each spring trails its target by damping * speed / stiffness (27 cm at 3.4 m/s) and the 5 springs add up. Teleport: SpringBone resets past 256 cm of error, SpringBoneChain3D past 1.5 m of root move or 1 m of error",
    "start": "the springs are placed on the Idle_Loop t = 0 pose by a zero-length evaluation before tick 1 (InitAnim's zero tick, SkeletalMeshComponent.cpp:1213-1216; the game builds SpringBoneChain3D on that pose)"
  },
